  - Pre-commit hook will automatically run all tests and block commits if any fail



  # Process Rule

  NEVER GIVE TIME ESTIMATES OR EFFORT ESTIMATES FOR HOW LONG A FEATURE WILL TAKE

  When a user asks you to make a code change, determine if it is trivial and can be done directly, or if it requires more careful consideration.


  ## Plan Rules
  - When making plans for multi file changes, always proceed with test driven development.

  ## Building Plan Rules
  - When you think you are done, test the changes u made (this is test driven development), while there is still errors, fix those erros. In order to mark the task complete and return back to the user, you must have a passing test along with your response.

  ## Context Management

  - **ALWAYS** keep context under 40% throughout work
  - When context is above that, let the user know a summarization would be helpful.

